// FUNCTION: BFME2 0x001415B0 size=140 name=?Insert@BFME2SceneSpatialIndex@@QAEXPAVRenderObjClass@@HHH@Z evidence=N:ledger
void BFME2SceneSpatialIndex::Insert(RenderObjClass *obj, int x, int y, int z)
{
	// Walk down from the root: each level splits a cell in four (x picks the
	// odd children, y the upper pair) until the object's size level is reached.
	CellClass *cell = Cells;
	unsigned int bit = Resolution >> 1;
	unsigned int span = CellCount >> 2;
	while (span != 0) {
		if (z & bit)
			break;
		cell->Count++;
		int child = ((x & bit) ? 1 : 0) + ((y & bit) ? 2 : 0);
		cell += child * span + 1;
		span >>= 2;
		bit >>= 1;
	}
	cell->Objects.Add(obj, false);
	obj->Set_Spatial_Cell((((x << 10) | y) << 10) | z);
}

// FUNCTION: BFME2 0x00141640 size=173 name=?Remove@BFME2SceneSpatialIndex@@QAEXPAVRenderObjClass@@@Z evidence=N:ledger
void BFME2SceneSpatialIndex::Remove(RenderObjClass *obj)
{
	int code = obj->Get_Spatial_Cell();
	int x = code >> 20;
	int y = (code >> 10) % 1024;
	int z = code % 1024;

	CellClass *cell = Cells;
	unsigned int bit = Resolution >> 1;
	unsigned int span = CellCount >> 2;
	while (span != 0) {
		if (z & bit)
			break;
		cell->Count--;
		int child = ((y & bit) ? 2 : 0) + ((x & bit) ? 1 : 0);
		cell += child * span + 1;
		span >>= 2;
		bit >>= 1;
	}
	cell->Objects.Remove(obj);
	obj->Set_Spatial_Cell(-1);
}

